  "translate_en|mods/SalvageWorks/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_ScrapSurvival_CraftingSpeed_tooltip": "Adjusts only the duration of Salvage Works crafting actions. Very Fast = quarter duration; Fast = half duration; Normal = intended duration; Slow = double duration. Vanilla recipes and recipes from other mods are not affected.",
  "translate_en|mods/SalvageWorks/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_ScrapSurvival_RecyclingYieldMultiplier": "Recycling Yield",
  "translate_en|mods/SalvageWorks/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_ScrapSurvival_RecyclingYieldMultiplier_tooltip": "Controls how many materials are recovered when recycling. 1.00 = normal yield, 0.50 = half yield, 2.00 = double yield. Item condition and the character’s relevant skill still influence the final result.",
  "translate_en|mods/SalvageWorks/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_ScrapSurvival_SkillRequirements": "Skill Requirements",
  "translate_en|mods/SalvageWorks/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_ScrapSurvival_SkillRequirements_tooltip": "Yes: Salvage Works recipes use their intended skill levels. No: skill levels do not block the mod's recipes. Materials, tools, and workstations are still required. After changing this option, in single-player quit and reload the game. In multiplayer, restart the server for the change to take effect."
